<title>INDIA: Indian soybean up, meal and oil steady.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean up, meal and oil steady.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices rose by 100-150 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Business volumes were good and the undertone was steady. Soyoil solvent was steady but soyoil refined rose by 100 rupees per tonne on good demand in local markets. Business volumes were dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were almost steady. Soymeal yellow was $283 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $110 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 3,800 rupees per tonne in FOR condition.</p>
